WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
Mark: Hi.

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:01.900
This is...

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:02.880
(quietly) what?

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:05.200
What'd you do?

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:07.140
Tyler: (through laughter)
I didn't do anything!

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.420
Mark: Hi. My name is Markiplier.

00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:13.580
(All laugh)

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:15.320
Mark: Ethan. This is Ethan.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:16.540
Ethan: (chuckles) Hey.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:17.540
Mark: CrankGame-
Ethan: First time.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.240
Mark: CrankGameplays.
Ethan: Nice to meet you.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.100
(All laugh)

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:21.220
Mark: This is Tyler.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.580
Uh... And we're gonna do
something really nice today.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:27.780
God, these are gro-- these nails
of mine are gross.

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.760
(All laugh)

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:38.380
Mark: So we're gonna be
doing something nice.

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:40.180
Something really like... fun.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.880
It's more of a craft thing.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:42.820
It's...

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:43.640
(high-pitched) N A I L S.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.540
(Ethan laughs)

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:48.920
Mark: Nails. So, the history of nails are...

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.780
Tyler: They're on you before you're born.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:55.840
And they... grow forever...

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.960
Calcium makes them stronger.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:59.200
And they're like bones... kind of.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.100
Ethan: (through laughter) Out of your tips.

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:05.420
Mark: And the history... (giggles)

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:08.580
Ethan: You're asking me?
Mark: .. of nail art. Yes.

00:01:08.820 --> 00:01:10.280
Ethan: Oh, of nail art.
Mark: Yeah.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:11.220
Ethan: Pablo Picasso.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:12.960
You know him. You love him.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:14.880
What was his first canvas?

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.440
His thumbnail right here.

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.340
I mean it was his thumbnail,
not mine, but you get it.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.340
He looked at himself and he said:

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.460
"You know, I want to start making art,"

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.480
"but I don't want to go big first."

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.560
"I'll start smaller, and work my way up."

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.280
And so, he went to work, little by little,

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.740
making his perfect little
masterpiece on his nail.

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:37.500
Until one day he said:

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.540
"Hey..."

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.680
"This might be nice to have... all the time."

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:44.880
Don't laugh at history.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.640
It's not funny. It's very serious.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.779
He's dead now.

00:01:48.779 --> 00:01:50.380
Don't be disrespectful.

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.440
Anyway, he said:

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.460
"Hey! That might be nice to do all the time."

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.040
So he went out, and people
saw his nails and went:

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:57.600
(inhales)

00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:00.900
"Pablo! How could you
do this without telling us?"

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:02.220
(Mark chuckles)

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:03.700
Ethan: And Pablo said:

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.060
'Cause he's... Spanish?

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:08.800
Right?

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:12.340
And they said:

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.840
"Pablo, Pablo, Pablo."

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.840
"You've really out-done yourself this time."

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:16.720
And he said:

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.280
And then from then on, it was history.

00:02:21.460 --> 00:02:25.260
Everyone's doing their nails, just like Pablo,
and just like the Pablo before him.

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:26.660
And... you know.

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.621
That's really where it came from.

00:02:28.621 --> 00:02:30.520
Mark: And there you have it everybody.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.460
Okay, so we got...

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.540
(Ethan and Tyler laughs)
Mark: nail stuff here. In front of us.

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:37.820
I've never done my nails.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.960
But my mom does nail art,

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:43.740
and she has decorated my nails
in a great way before.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:44.520
(inhales)

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.280
I don't remember how that
happened, but um...

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:48.040
I take nothing from that...

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.980
But we have stuff here.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:51.540
It's been carefully picked out.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.680
Everything we need to make
fantastic nail art is right here.

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:55.440
These are the rules:

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:57.120
You only have to decorate one hand.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:02:58.660
But it has to have a theme,

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:00.580
or at least you need to
explain the theme.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:02.560
What it is, what you're
trying to accomplish.

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:05.440
It's OK if you don't have, like,
a lot of artistic ability,

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.080
so we're not looking for, like,
drawings on the nail.

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.660
But it has to have a theme
across the entire hand.

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:10.660
Mark: Make sense?
Ethan: Mm-hm.

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:12.560
Mark: And that's it. You can
use whatever you want...

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:13.740
We have ten minutes.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.140
And then after the ten
minutes, we will judge.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:16.860
Mark:Makes sense?
Ethan: Makes sense.

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.420
Mark: Can I get ten minutes on the clock?

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:19.580
Amy: Three, two, one, go!

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:21.140
Mark: Oh!
Ethan: Oookay!

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:22.760
Mark: First... (rubs nail file)

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.840
Ethan: Ooooh. Good idea.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.600
Mark: I've seen this before. I've seen this... 
Ethan: Good idea.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:27.020
Mark: I imagine to get a rough surface...

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:28.700
Ethan: OH! I don't like that.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.580
(All laugh)

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.320
(Elephant-like roar)

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.800
Ethan: I don't like the feeling of this.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:36.240
(Boom)

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.820
Mark: OK, I've really ground them
down into a fine powder.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:43.140
It's really powdery right now.
I think that's a good first step.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.600
I want the pigment of my nail to mix
with the polish, and really...

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.660
really shine through.
(Ethan dying)

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.500
Ethan: (through laughter)
Is this supposed to hurt?

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:51.980
Mark: I know. I know this.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:53.900
This... ah... THIS is supposed to hurt!

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.040
'Cause you gotta push...

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.440
You gotta, like... push your cuticles back
or something like that.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:03:59.440
Ethan: [distorted] OOOHH

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:01.540
Mark: I think that I remember my mom
doing this, and I was like:

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:02.540
"This is horrible!" And she's like:

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:03.600
"Oh, shut up, you big baby."

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:04.600
(from "Momiplier Does My Nails")
Momiplier: What are you doing now?

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:05.100
Mark: Ow.

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.400
Meme insert: SHUT YOUR FUCKING MOUTH.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.020
Mark: My mom's gonna be so ashamed of me.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.120
Ah... My mom is always ashamed of me.

00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:11.840
Mark: The hell is this?

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:13.300
What is this?

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:14.520
What is this??

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:15.260
What?

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:16.960
What is this?

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.440
Mark: Well, it says that but...

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:20.420
What?

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:21.880
(smack)

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:22.380
Mark: Wait...

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:24.520
(Ethan laughs)

00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:31.720
Mark: BUT WHAT IS IT?

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.960
Mark: I've thrown the box away, I can't, uh...

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.200
What is this?

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.200
What is this? Is it, like, a dog tag?

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:41.200
Ethan: How many times?

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:42.640
Mark: Shut up!

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.060
Ethan: I'm going to go with
this holographic look.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.020
Shake it up first.

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:47.440
Oh, yes...

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:49.440
My nails are going to look good.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:50.880
Mark: I'm gonna do the marbling...

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:55.340
Mark: [mockingly] You need to
do multiple colors!

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:57.060
There's multiple colors in this one!

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.700
I'm sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:01.400
Oh, yeah, that's good.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:04.180
(Ethan and Mark giggles)

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.260
Mark: What have I done?

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.340
I think to marble, you need
like, more than one color.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:10.340
Ethan: What have you done?

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:10.940
Mark: Shush.

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.240
Magic. Beauty. Grace.

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.160
Everything above.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.220
Mark: Why is there like
a film on the top of--

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:17.060
WHAT IS THIS?!

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:17.860
UH!

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:18.460
UAH!

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.260
UUUUAAAH.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:20.460
Mark: I've got a good start.

00:05:21.040 --> 00:05:25.540
I've just gonna clean the snot-like
substance off of my other fingers.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.920
So, you know, this is the start.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:29.120
How much time do we have?

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.880
Amy: Three minutes.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:32.160
Mark: Alright, excellent!

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.200
Ethan: Wait, we have three minutes?

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.680
Mark: Yeah yeah yeah yeah yeah,
we're gonna get to it!

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:38.020
Three minutes guys, GO!

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.640
Hyperspeed! You don't have time!

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:42.940
We don't have time to go around anywhere.

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:44.620
Ethan: OH. MY. GOD!

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.060
YOU HIT MY ELBOW!

00:05:46.060 --> 00:05:47.380
Mark: IT'S NOT MY FAULT!

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.040
(spits)

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:50.560
Ethan: (whines) Oh my god, it was
so good, now it's ruined.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.500
Mark: I don't believe it was
good before, anyway.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.000
What... the... heck?

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:56.780
WHAT THE-? Oh! Okay.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:57.800
(whispers) I get it.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:58.600
Ethan: Look at mine.

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:00.960
Mark: Yeah, I don't wanna
look at your ugly hand.

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:02.940
Ethan: I'M not talking to you!

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:08.740
(Mark breaths heavily)
(Heartbeats and high-pitched ringing)

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.140
(Tyler wheezes)

00:06:10.560 --> 00:06:11.440
Ethan: You okay?

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:12.120
Mark: Yeah, I'm fine.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.120
Ethan: My nails look like a toddler did them.

00:06:14.120 --> 00:06:16.120
How do yours look?

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:17.400
(Ethan wheezes like an asthma attack)

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:19.400
Ethan: Oh my god.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.540
Mark: Alright, I'm good.
What's the time at?

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:22.280
Amy: Two seconds.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.400
Tyler: Wait, what?

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.820
Mark: Alright!

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:27.340
Tyler: How is that enough time to do art?

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.620
Amy: I know! That's what I'm saying!

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:29.640
Mark: No what? We're done!

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.540
Mark: I did I [unintelligible]

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.760
Tyler: I mean I did a multi-layered one...

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:36.380
Ethan: I think as far as the theme goes...

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:38.900
Ethan's got a theme down.

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:41.460
Tyler: You just colored them all
in the exact same nail polish.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:43.140
Yeah, that's a theme, uh.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.000
UH!

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:44.900
Mark: I...

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:48.980
Went way above and beyond. I call it
a well-marbled Christmas.

00:06:48.980 --> 00:06:51.720
Marble is real hard to do, cuz...

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:54.740
It gets real sticky on the top.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:56.140
It kind of wrapped around my finger.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:59.220
In terms of like overall quality
is pretty good, right?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.300
Ethan: I think it's pretty good.

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.143
Mark: Alright fair enough.

00:07:05.143 --> 00:07:06.180
Ethan: I don't think so either.

00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:07.780
Mark: Alright. So explain yours.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.000
Tyler: Well, I didn't finish mine
but it was gonna be glim and glam

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.620
cuz everything's gonna be
glittery and fancy..

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.520
glim and glam.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:17.000
Mark: Alright, okay. So that was the trial run.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:18.206
Everyone feel good about that?

00:07:18.206 --> 00:07:19.620
Ethan: I feel fairly good.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.440
Mark: So, that was just practice,
cuz none of us know how to do this.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:24.300
None of us.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:27.600
All of us failed across the board.
Not a single one of us succeeded.

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:31.540
This is why... we were given two hands.

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.480
I feel like someone they're gonna be mad for me saying that.

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:38.280
So, we have another shot at this, okay?

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:39.340
Tyler, stop!

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:40.120
Put your ink down!

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.420
Tyler listen to ME!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.260
TYLER YOU NEVER LISTEN TO ME!

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.400
Put it down!

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:45.500
YOU TOO! (spits)

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:46.680
We're gonna go at this again.

00:07:46.840 --> 00:07:49.420
This time we'll get twenty minutes.

00:07:49.420 --> 00:07:50.660
Does that sound fair?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.360
Ethan: Wow...

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:51.860
Twenty minutes.

00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:54.200
Mark: No you have to start over.

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:56.080
Mark: Right hand.

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.080
Tyler: I-- No!

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.020
Mark: You're at the advantage!
Tyler: No!

00:07:59.020 --> 00:08:00.540
Mark: You're the only one
that's ambidextrous!

00:08:02.840 --> 00:08:05.200
Tyler: No it isn't! It is
distinctly different!

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.680
Mark: All in favor of it being
the same thing, say aye.

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:07.680
Mark, Ethan and Amy: Aye.

00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:09.420
Tyler: IT'S NOT!

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.220
Mark: All opposed?

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:13.220
Tyler: ME! The only person who
has the right to vote in this!

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:13.720
Mark: Alright.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.240
Well, the only person with the right
to vote didn't vote correctly.

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:18.180
They said "me" instead of "nay".

00:08:18.180 --> 00:08:19.680
The motion has passed.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.960
That was democracy in action,
just because you--

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.960
Tyler: Democracy is a
failure as a government.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:26.620
Mark: Oh, well, that's another
topic for another day. (All laugh)

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.980
Alright, so we're gonna
try again, okay? Ready?

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:30.980
Ethan: Yes.

00:08:31.180 --> 00:08:32.460
Mark: Three, two, one,

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:33.680
have at it.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:34.860
Ethan: Oooo....

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.400
I didn't think of a theme.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:41.860
Are you confident?

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:42.760
Mark: Yeah, I feel good about this.

00:08:42.760 --> 00:08:46.900
I've got an idea, and I think it's
gonna come across like pretty cool.

00:08:47.040 --> 00:08:51.560
But I mean like, well I need like hope
or something if it's actually gonna work.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:52.620
Ethan: Oh are you doing it?

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:54.640
Are you doing the stamp?

00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:56.420
Mark: Wait is didn't...

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:57.140
What?

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.680
I didn't know that!

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.360
Oh no!

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:05.460
OH NOOO!

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:06.400
Okay it's fine.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:09.040
Yeah kinda but it'll be okay.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:09.923
It'll be even better now.

00:09:09.923 --> 00:09:10.920
It's okay, it's okay, it's alright...

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:12.880
(hands whoosh)

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:17.020
Mark: YOU just look bad.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:23.960
Tyler: See, the tricky part is to do more
stuff, you gotta wait for it to dry.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.160
Mark: Not me I say. Full steam ahead!

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:30.040
Mark: Ah it's not the worst thing in the world?
Ethan: A little bit of red...

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.380
Huf! UH!

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:40.800
Amy: You're half way through.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:41.720
Ethan: I'm all done.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:42.520
Can I keep mine a secret?

